Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Watching Two Axes at Once: Non-Commuting Continuous Measurement in the \
Quantum-Bayesian Picture\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["A single detector watching one axis of a qubit \
collapses it: the populations follow Bayes' rule and the coherence rides \
along in closed form, exactly the sibling essay's story. Point a second \
detector at a different axis and that closed form breaks, because the two \
Bayesian kicks are Gaussian operators that do not commute. This essay builds \
the general update from primitives and runs it: we watch the single-axis \
update stay diagonal, watch the two kicks fail to commute by a rotation about \
the third axis, and then let the general update take over. We watch the state \
stop collapsing and start diffusing, walk the measurement angle from collapse \
through localized diffusion to an isotropic random walk on the Bloch sphere \
that never lands, read a purity ceiling set by detector efficiency, and \
finally pull the two closed-form output correlators back out of simulated \
records, where the cross-correlator at zero lag reads the cosine of the angle \
between the two watched axes. A last step connects this one-qubit toy to the \
gauge qubit of a Bacon-Shor code, whose error syndromes are exactly these \
cross-correlators.",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: August 18, 2026)", "Text",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Essay Flows", "Section",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["\<\
This essay is a computation-first tour of one qubit watched by two linear \
detectors at the same time, along two different Bloch-sphere axes: how the \
single-axis Bayesian update is a closed form on the populations, why a \
second, non-commuting axis destroys that closed form, what the general update \
does instead, how the collapse gives way to persistent diffusion as the two \
axes separate, why the uncertainty principle forbids the diffusion from ever \
stopping, and how the two noisy output records carry the whole story in their \
temporal correlators. Every claim is computed on the spot from base Wolfram \
Language, so nothing here rests on a formula you cannot immediately test and \
change.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["\<\
In other words, I have tried to build a small laboratory for simultaneous \
measurement of incompatible observables. I strongly believe in a \
computation-first narrative for learning: in a sense, if I cannot compute it, \
I cannot claim to understand it. The rhythm throughout is concept, then \
computation, then interpretation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["\<\
The environment you see is a live Wolfram notebook. Evaluate the cells from \
top to bottom; the toolkit defined in the next section is used by every \
section that follows, so those dependencies matter. Two of the cells run \
Monte-Carlo ensembles and take a minute or two; I flag them where they \
appear. My suggestion is to focus on the output and its meaning first, then \
unpack the input code. You are not locked into any of it: change the angle, \
the rates, the seed, and rerun your own experiments.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the non-commuting door into the same continuous-measurement physics \
that the core essay, ",
 Cell["Korotkov-Quantum-Bayesian.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 ", treats for a single symmetric detector. That essay is the prerequisite: \
it builds the Gaussian likelihood, the Bayes kick on the populations with the \
coherence riding along, and the purity ride-along that we here watch break. \
We recall its single-axis update in Section 1 and then generalize."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell["\<\
Notation and Conventions: Two Detectors, Two Records, One Qubit\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We work in units where the reduced Planck constant is one, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 ". The qubit is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 " density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\\", "openone"}], "+", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "+", 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "+", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 ", with real Bloch coordinates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 ". Two linear detectors watch two directions on the Bloch sphere at the same \
time: the first watches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 ", the second watches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]", "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 ", an axis lying in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 "-plane at angle ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 ". The two produce noisy output records,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    StyleBox["Tr",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Tr",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SqrtBox[
       StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], " ", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 " independent white noises, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 ". We assume phase-sensitive amplifiers on the optimal quadrature, so there \
is no phase back-action, only the informational (quantum-Bayesian) kind. Two \
numbers per channel organize everything: the ensemble dephasing rate ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalGamma]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 " that measurement imposes, and the detector efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "\[Element]"}], "(", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 ", related to the collapse time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[CapitalGamma]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 "; an ideal (quantum-limited) detector has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[CapitalGamma]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 ". When we average a record over a step ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 ", the reading has Gaussian window variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "/", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[CapitalGamma]", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 " for an ideal detector. We take the two channels equally strong, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "\[CurlyPhi]"], "=", "\[CapitalGamma]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],
 ", unless we say otherwise."
}], "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Fix the two measured directions and the readouts we will plot: the angled \
observable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 ", the Bloch vector, the purity, and the Bloch length:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "sigmaPhi", ",", " ", "blochVec", ",", " ", "purity", ",", " ", "rlen"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", "phi_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "phi", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochVec", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "j", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"purity", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rlen", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
   RowBox[{"blochVec", "[", "rho", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Bloch length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["r",
       FontWeight->"Bold",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["y", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " is one for a pure state and shrinks toward zero for a mixed one, so it is \
the single number that tells us whether the record is monitoring an actual \
wavefunction or only an ensemble."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the object the whole essay turns on. Recall from the core essay that \
measuring a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 "-valued observable and reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 " over a step multiplies the state, in the eigenbasis of that observable, by \
the square roots of the two Gaussian likelihoods. That element-wise \
multiplication is exactly conjugation by a single operator: a Gaussian Kraus \
operator that is a matrix function of the measured Pauli. Encode it, for a \
reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " of a Pauli ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],
 " with window variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "kraus", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ibar_", ",", " ", "A_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"ibar", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], " ", "A"}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"\\", "openone"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 ", this exponential is just ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cosh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   RowBox[{"\\", "openone"}], "+", 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 ": a single Hermitian operator built from the measured axis, applied as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"M", "\[Rho]", "M"}], "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 ". This one object is the whole update, and everything downstream is what \
happens when we build it out of two non-commuting axes."
}], "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell["\<\
Define the honest detector draw, sampling a reading from the two-outcome \
Gaussian mixture that the current state predicts for the measured observable:\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "drawRead", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"drawRead", "[", 
   RowBox[{"rho_", ",", " ", "A_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
  "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Clip", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
             RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
              RowBox[{"A", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
          "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
             RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
              RowBox[{"A", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
          "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "1."}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dvar", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In words, the detector first picks which eigenvalue to ring, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 ", with the Born weights ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "\[PlusMinus]", 
    StyleBox["Tr",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"A", "\[Rho]"}], "TI"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
 ", then buries the level under Gaussian window noise of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 "; the two channels draw independently from the same state."
}], "Text",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell["1. One Axis: The Closed Form We Are About to Break", "Section",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start with a single detector on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 ", which is the core essay's whole story. Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 " is diagonal, its Kraus operator is diagonal too, so the update touches the \
two populations and the two coherences separately: the populations pick up \
the Gaussian likelihood ratio and renormalize (classical Bayes), and the \
coherence rides along on the geometric mean. There is nothing to solve. Look \
at the single-axis Kraus operator:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ibar", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", "//",
   " ", "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, it is diagonal, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", "2", 
      StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", "2", 
      StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 ": measuring one axis is a scaling of the two amplitudes in that axis's own \
basis, and the population ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " simply multiplies by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 ". This is why the single-axis update has a closed form, and why a pure \
state stays pure along a single record. The next question is what a second, \
differently pointed detector does to this tidy diagonal picture."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell["2. Two Axes: Why the Closed Form Breaks", "Section",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A second detector on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 " contributes its own Gaussian Kraus operator, diagonal in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 " basis rather than the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 " basis. To apply both over one step we must multiply the two operators, and \
the order matters unless they commute. They do not, and the failure is not a \
small correction: it is the entire reason simultaneous non-commuting \
measurement is a distinct physical process. Compute the commutator of the two \
single-axis kicks for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", 
    ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
     RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], 
   " ", "-", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
     RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", 
    ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The commutator is nonzero and off-diagonal, so there is no basis in which \
both kicks are diagonal at once, and therefore no closed-form population \
update: the two detectors cannot be reduced to two independent Bayesian \
scalings. Confirm that the mismatch is exactly a kick about the third axis, \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], 
      " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
       RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], 
     " ", "-", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
       RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], 
      " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}]}],
     " ", "==", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "I", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sinh", "[", 
      RowBox[{"a", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sinh", "[", 
      RowBox[{"b", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"b", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two kicks fail to commute by a rotation about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],
 ", inheriting the algebra ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 " of the observables they measure. Because the mismatch is first order in \
each reading, it scales like the step, so the two orderings agree as the step \
shrinks; but at any finite step the joint measurement genuinely mixes the two \
channels, and we must carry the full ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 " matrix."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The general update takes over. It is the entire step: draw both readings \
from the current state, apply the two Bayesian kicks as a symmetric split \
(half the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 "-kick, the full ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 "-kick, half the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 "-kick), and renormalize. Define it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "measureStepNC", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"measureStepNC", "[", 
    RowBox[{"phi_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=",
   " ", 
  RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"szA", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"spA", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "ibz", ",", " ", 
      "ibp", ",", " ", "mm", ",", " ", "r1"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ibz", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"drawRead", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "szA", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
     
     RowBox[{"ibp", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"drawRead", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "spA", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n",
      "   ", 
     RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ibz", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "szA", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
        "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
       RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ibp", ",", " ", "spA", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", ".", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ibz", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "szA", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
        "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"r1", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mm", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "mm", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"r1", "/", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "r1", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That is the whole integrator: two Gaussian draws, three matrix products for \
the symmetric split, and one renormalization, with no basis in which it \
factors into scalar Bayes rules. Confirm it keeps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 " a physical state, trace one and Hermitian, after a step from a generic \
mixed state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"r0", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.6", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"0.2", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0.1", " ", "I"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"0.2", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0.1", " ", "I"}]}], ",", " ", "0.4"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"r1", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "1", "]"}], ";", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"measureStepNC", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "5."}], "]"}], "[", "r0", 
          "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Chop", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "r1", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HermitianMatrixQ", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Chop", "@", "r1"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell["\<\
As expected, the step preserves the trace and Hermiticity: the general update \
is a legitimate quantum operation even though it is not a closed-form Bayes \
rule.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell["\<\
3. Orthogonal Axes: The State Stops Collapsing and Starts Diffusing\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Point the second detector at right angles to the first, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 ", so the two watched axes are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 ", maximally incompatible. Now each detector is forever trying to collapse \
the state onto its own axis while the other detector pulls it away, and \
neither wins: instead of localizing to a pole, the pure state performs a \
persistent random walk. On the ideal detectors it never leaves the surface of \
the Bloch sphere, because information gain alone does not decohere a single \
record, so the walk is along a great circle. Run one orthogonal-measurement \
trajectory from the fully mixed center and watch the Bloch coordinates:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "800"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dvar", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"tt", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "800"}], "]"}], " ", "0.02"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"traj", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "4", "]"}], ";", "\n", "       ", 
           RowBox[{"blochVec", " ", "/@", " ", 
            RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"measureStepNC", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              "nst"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "traj", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<y\>\"", ",", 
            " ", "\"\<z\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma])\>\"", ",", 
            " ", "\"\<Bloch vector\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
         "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
          " ", "\"\<orthogonal measurement: persistent diffusion, no collapse\
\>\""}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 " coordinates wander over the whole range and never settle, while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 " stays near zero: the state diffuses on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 " great circle, driven back and forth by the two competing records. There is \
no pole to fall into, so the \"collapse\" of the single-axis case is replaced \
by a walk that never ends. See it as a path on the sphere by plotting the \
same trajectory in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 "-plane against the unit circle:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "800"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dvar", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"traj", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "4", "]"}], ";", "\n", "       ", 
           RowBox[{"blochVec", " ", "/@", " ", 
            RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"measureStepNC", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              "nst"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "1.1"}], ",", " ", "1.1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "1.1"}], ",", " ", "1.1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<z\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{
         "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
          " ", "\"\<the same record as a walk on the xz great circle\>\""}], ",",
          "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Circle", "[", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "380"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],

Cell["\<\
The path hugs the unit circle, wandering around it without a preferred point: \
the two orthogonal detectors together monitor the wavefunction perfectly (it \
stays pure) while leaving its position on the great circle to diffuse freely. \
This is the isotropic persistent diffusion that the single-basis picture has \
no room for.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],

Cell["\<\
4. Turning the Angle: From Collapse to Localized Diffusion to a Free Walk\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The angle ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 " between the two watched axes tunes the whole character of the motion. At \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 " the two detectors watch the same axis, their kicks commute (both \
diagonal), and the state collapses to a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],
 "-pole exactly as one strong measurement would. As ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],
 " opens up, the state can no longer reach a single point, but the axes still \
leave an imprint: it localizes to regions near the two eigen-directions and \
jitters there. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 " the imprint vanishes and the walk is uniform. Watch this by running an \
ensemble from the center for three angles and reading, at the end of each \
run, how far the state sits from the equator, the mean of ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 ", keyed by the angle (this cell runs a small ensemble and takes a few \
seconds):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.03"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "250"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "200"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dvar", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
           RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"100", " ", "phi"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "k"}], 
                "]"}], ";", "\n", "        ", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"blochVec", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"Last", "@", 
                  RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"measureStepNC", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ",
                     "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
         "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 " the mean of ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],
 " is one (the state has collapsed to a pole), at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 " it drops to an intermediate value (localized but pulled toward the poles), \
and at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 " it settles near the value a uniform point on the great circle would give, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "/", "\[Pi]", "\[TildeTilde]", "0.64"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 ": the axes have stopped imprinting and the walk has gone isotropic. The \
transition is smooth in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],
 ", from collapse through localized diffusion to a free walk, and, as the \
great-circle path of Section 3 already showed, the Bloch length holds at one \
throughout because purity is untouched."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell["5. The Uncertainty Floor: Why the Diffusion Cannot Stop", "Section",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There is a reason the state can never settle once the axes differ. For it \
to stop, both detectors would have to fall silent at the same instant, that \
is, the state would have to be a still point for both measurement \
back-actions at once. A single measurement has two such points, its two \
eigenstates. Two non-commuting measurements share none, and the uncertainty \
principle is exactly the statement that the total measurement disturbance is \
bounded below by their commutator. For a qubit the disturbance per step is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2"], "+", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]", "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", "\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 ", the sum of the two variances, and the bound is the magnitude of the \
commutator. Confirm, for any pure state, that the sum of variances can never \
fall below the commutator magnitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["z", "TI"]], ",", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "=", "2", GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["y", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"z", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "y", "]"}]}]}], " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"y", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"z", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"y", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"z", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The inequality holds everywhere and, written as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{GridBox[{
        {
         StyleBox["y", "TI"]}
       },
       GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
       GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],
 ", saturates only at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["y", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 ": the disturbance vanishes only if the state points fully along ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 ", which is a still point for neither the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 " nor the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],
 " detector but the direction that carries zero signal in both. Away from \
that single unreachable direction the disturbance is strictly positive, so \
the state is always being kicked, and the diffusion of Section 3 is a direct \
consequence of the uncertainty principle rather than a numerical artifact."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A real detector loses some of the information it gathers, and that loss \
caps how pure the state can be kept. With efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 " per channel the coherence is bled faster than the two records sharpen it, \
so the isotropic walk settles onto a sphere of radius less than one. The \
steady radius is set entirely by the efficiency. First encode the non-ideal \
loss as a pure-dephasing factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 " on the coherence about a measured axis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "dephaseAxis", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dephaseAxis", "[", 
   RowBox[{"rho_", ",", " ", "A_", ",", " ", "gt_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "A"}], 
         ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"q", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "A"}], 
         ")"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", "p"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"q", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", "q"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"-", "gt"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"rho", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", "p"}], " ", "-", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"q", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", "q"}]}], 
       ")"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This shrinks only the part of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 " that is off-diagonal in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 "-basis, leaving the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 "-populations alone, which is exactly the information the detector gathered \
but failed to deliver. Now add this loss to each of the two channels after \
the Bayesian kick, and read the steady Bloch length for three efficiencies, \
keyed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 " (this cell runs a small ensemble and takes a few seconds):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "600"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "150"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dvar", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.64", ",", " ", "0.36"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"With", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"gt", " ", "=", " ", 
             RowBox[{"gm", " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"1.", "/", "eta"}], " ", "-", " ", "1."}], ")"}], " ",
               "dt"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"With", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"step", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
                RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"dephaseAxis", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"dephaseAxis", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"measureStepNC", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], "[", 
                    "rho", "]"}], ",", "\n", "          ", 
                    RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "gt"}], 
                    "]"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "gt"}], 
                  "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
             RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
              RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"1000", " ", "eta"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "k"}],
                    "]"}], ";", "\n", "         ", 
                  RowBox[{"rlen", "@", 
                   RowBox[{"Last", "@", 
                    RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"step", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ",
                     "nst"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
            "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.64", ",", " ", "0.36"}], "}"}]}], 
          "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As expected, the steady radius tracks ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 ": only the ideal detector holds the state on the surface, and below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],
 " the isotropic walk settles onto a smaller sphere whose radius drops as the \
square root of the efficiency. The lost information is the gap between \
monitoring an actual wavefunction and monitoring only its blurred image."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell["6. The Output Correlators and the Cosine at Zero Lag", "Section",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the payoff. The state itself is hard to see, but the two records ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],
 " are right there, and their temporal correlators carry the physics in \
closed form. Korotkov and Atalaya derived the self- and cross-correlators of \
the two output signals directly from the Bayesian equations, and for equally \
strong ideal channels with no extra evolution they are sums of two decaying \
exponentials with rates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "\[MinusPlus]", 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 ". Encode the closed forms:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"kzzCF", ",", " ", "kzpCF"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"kzzCF", "[", 
    RowBox[{"phi_", ",", " ", "gm_", ",", " ", "tau_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], 
    " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}]}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kzpCF", "[", 
   RowBox[{"phi_", ",", " ", "gm_", ",", " ", "tau_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}], " ",
       "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], 
     ")"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}], "/", "2"}], ")"}], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}], " ",
       "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], 
     ")"}]}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],

Cell["\<\
Read the two limits that these forms make vivid: the self-correlator starts \
at one and the cross-correlator starts at the cosine of the angle between the \
axes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"kzzCF", "[", 
     RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "gm", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"kzpCF", "[", 
     RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "gm", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The self-correlator at zero lag is one and the cross-correlator at zero lag \
is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],
 ": aligned detectors (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],
 ") see perfectly correlated records, orthogonal detectors (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 ") see uncorrelated ones, and the cosine interpolates. This is a purely \
dynamical readout of the angle between two incompatible measurements, \
available without ever reconstructing the state."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell["\<\
Now recover these closed forms from the records themselves. Run an ensemble \
of orthogonal-and-angled measurement records, form the \
ensemble-and-time-averaged two-time correlators, and overlay the closed \
forms. First define a run that emits both readings while it measures:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "recordNC", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"recordNC", "[", 
   RowBox[{"phi_", ",", " ", "dvar_", ",", " ", "nst_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], 
   "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"szA", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"spA", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        "ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "mm"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"ibz", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"drawRead", "[", 
            RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "szA", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"ibp", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"drawRead", "[", 
            RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "spA", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
          "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ibz", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "szA", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
             "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
            RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
             RowBox[{"ibp", ",", " ", "spA", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
             " ", 
            RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ibz", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "szA", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
             "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"mm", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "mm", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
          RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"rho", "/", 
            RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "rho", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", "ibp"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "nst", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],

Cell["\<\
Each step appends the two readings while the same readings drive the Bayesian \
kick, so the records and the state share the very same noise, which is what \
makes the cross-correlator carry the back-action. Now simulate two angles and \
compare with the closed form (this is the heavy cell, an ensemble of records \
for each angle; it takes a couple of minutes):\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "250"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "1000"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nlag", " ", "=", " ", "10"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"phis", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dvar", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", "taus", ",",
        " ", "mc", ",", " ", "cf"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"taus", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nlag", "]"}], " ", "dt"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"mc", "[", "phi_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"recs", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"recordNC", "[", 
              RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "nst", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"700", " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"100", " ", "phi"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "k"}]}], 
              "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
         "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
              RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"#", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
                    RowBox[{"#", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"t", " ", "+", " ", "j"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
                   " ", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"nst", " ", "-", " ", "j"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
                 " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "recs"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "nlag"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
           "     ", 
           RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
              RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"#", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"t", " ", "+", " ", "j"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
                    RowBox[{"#", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"nst", " ", "-", " ", "j"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
                 " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "recs"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "nlag"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
        "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ListPlot", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"taus", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"mc", "[", "phi", "]"}], "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                
                RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"taus", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"mc", "[", "phi", "]"}], "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
               " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "phis"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            "1"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"nlag", " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "0.1"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
           "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<lag \[Tau] (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma])\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<output correlator\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<K_zz, \[Phi]=\[Pi]/4\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<K_z\[Phi], \[Phi]=\[Pi]/4\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<K_zz, \[Phi]=\[Pi]/2\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<K_z\[Phi], \[Phi]=\[Pi]/2\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
          "    ", 
          RowBox[{
          "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
           " ", "\"\<simulated records recover the closed-form \
correlators\>\""}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
        "   ", 
        RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Evaluate", "@", 
           RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
            RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"kzzCF", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",",
                 " ", 
                RowBox[{"kzpCF", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], 
               "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "phis"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"tau", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"nlag", " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
       "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each simulated correlator sits on its closed-form curve: the \
self-correlators decay from one, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 " cross-correlator starts near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[TildeTilde]", "0.71"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 " and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 " cross-correlator starts near zero, exactly the cosine law read off from \
the records. The state was never reconstructed; the angle between the two \
incompatible measurements is written directly in how their noisy outputs \
correlate."
}], "Text",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],

Cell["7. Reading a Hidden Rotation, and the Bacon-Shor Connection", "Section",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One last use of the correlators, and one last connection. If a small \
unwanted rotation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "~"], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 " about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],
 " is present, it breaks the symmetry between the two orderings and shows up \
only in the antisymmetrized cross-correlator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],
 ", which is otherwise zero. That difference is a sensitive probe of a \
rotation far too slow to see directly. Show that the difference is \
proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "~"], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],
 ", vanishing when the rotation does:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Gp", " ", "=", " ", "1.6"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.4"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.5"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"phi", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "om", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "phi", "]"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"Gp", " ", "-", " ", "Gm"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "Gm"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "Gp"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"om", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With no rotation the antisymmetrized cross-correlator is zero, and with a \
small rotation it is nonzero and grows linearly with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "~"], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],
 ": averaging many records turns a small, otherwise invisible frequency \
mismatch into a clearly measurable difference signal. In the experiment that \
grounds this theory, a residual Rabi frequency of a few kilohertz riding on a \
forty-megahertz drive was read out this way."
}], "Text",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell["\<\
The whole toy has a direct afterlife. A four-qubit Bacon-Shor code measures \
four two-qubit gauge operators continuously, and because two pairs of them do \
not commute, the encoded state carries a spare degree of freedom, a gauge \
qubit, that is measured along two orthogonal axes at once, exactly as here: \
it diffuses on a great circle while the logical qubit rides untouched. The \
code's error syndromes are then nothing but the cross-correlators of Section \
6, positive when the code is clean and flipping sign when an error moves the \
state to a subspace where the two watched axes have swapped orientation. The \
nine-qubit error-correcting version watches twelve gauge operators and reads \
its syndromes from triple correlators of three records at a time. The \
one-qubit cross-correlator we pulled out of simulated noise is, in that \
setting, a continuously monitored error check.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us (and What Comes Next)", "Section",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell["\<\
You now have a complete, computation-first toolkit for one qubit under two \
simultaneous non-commuting detectors: a Gaussian Kraus operator built from \
any measured axis, a symbolic proof that two such operators fail to commute \
by a rotation about the third axis, a general update that carries the full \
matrix where the single-axis closed form cannot, the transition from collapse \
through localized diffusion to an isotropic random walk as the axes separate, \
an uncertainty floor that forbids the walk from ever stopping, a purity \
ceiling set by efficiency, and two output correlators whose zero-lag \
cross-value reads the cosine of the angle between the watched axes. Before \
moving on, the points that were computed and verified along the way:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell["\<\
Measuring one axis is conjugation by a diagonal Gaussian Kraus operator, so \
the single-axis update stays a closed-form Bayes rule on the populations with \
the coherence riding along.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two axes' Kraus operators fail to commute by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 ", inheriting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],
 "; there is no basis diagonalizing both, hence no closed-form population \
update."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],

Cell["\<\
Orthogonal detectors keep a pure state pure while forcing it to diffuse on a \
great circle, replacing collapse with a persistent walk that never lands.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The angle ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 " tunes the motion from collapse (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],
 ") through localized diffusion to an isotropic walk (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],
 "), with the Bloch length untouched throughout."
}], "Item",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The measurement disturbance is bounded below by the commutator magnitude, \
saturating only along the unreadable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 "-direction, so the diffusion is a consequence of the uncertainty principle; \
efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],
 " caps the steady radius at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The output self- and cross-correlators are sums of exponentials with rates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "\[MinusPlus]", 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 "; at zero lag ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"z", "z"}], "TI"]], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"}]], "=", 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],
 ", recoverable directly from simulated records."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell["\<\
The antisymmetrized cross-correlator reads a hidden slow rotation; the same \
cross-correlators are the error syndromes of a Bacon-Shor code whose gauge \
qubit is exactly this doubly-watched qubit.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The natural continuations are the pieces this essay set aside: a phase \
back-action term that tilts the diffusion off the great circle, the finite \
detector bandwidth that couples the qubit to a cavity field, real-time \
feedback that locks the walk, and, in place of one qubit's two axes, two \
qubits watched jointly, whose measurement-induced entanglement is the subject \
of the sibling essay ",
 Cell["Watching-Two-Qubits.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
